<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="44857" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ME/598/44857.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="ME" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ME.xml">Mechanical Engineering</subject><course id="598" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ME/598.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>INC</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Laser 3D Printing</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>The course addresses laser powder bed fusion (LPBD) 3D printing technology. The LPBF is an additive manufacturing (AM) process where a laser fuses particulate materials such as metals, polymers, or ceramics. The course includes an overview of the LPBD method, data preparation workflow, AM process chain, AM parameters-microstructure-property relations, post-processing, and case studies. EOS company will offer a summer internship to a top student in the class.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to MENG:Mechanical Enginerng-UIUC.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="OLC">Online Lecture</type><start>ARRANGED</start><instructors><instructor lastName="Jasiuk" firstName="I">Jasiuk, I</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>